From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] Create, allocate and submit without waiting for the
 device

With guest-assigned handles, a create no longer drains earlier deferred replies
before it is sent, so it never pays the previous command's round trip.
vkAllocateMemory is sent without waiting when the allocation is plain and
leaves its heap at most half committed (caboose-bounded-memory/
async_allocation.h); otherwise a real VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY still
reaches the application. Queue submits defer their result as a checked reply.
Before the WSI surface socket names objects or work from this stream, the
encoder drains replies through the last pending create or submit
(drainObjects), leaving later fence waits pending. Time spent draining earlier
replies is reported by CABOOSE_READ_PROFILE as drainN.
